index c07f2e5..d8673e5 100644
--- a/docs/runbooks/DEPLOY.md
+++ b/docs/runbooks/DEPLOY.md
@@ -44,6 +44,47 @@ A full deploy smoke test (anonymous sign-in → socket join → session id) is
 described in the deployment evidence under `evidence/`; `scripts/verify-all.sh`
 must be green before deploying.
 
+## Launch attestation (owner detached signature)
+
+SEC-P1-001: the launch gate no longer accepts a committed approval sentence.
+The owner supplies, out-of-band:
+
+- `LAUNCH_OWNER_PUBLIC_KEY` — PEM public key.
+- `LAUNCH_OWNER_SIGNATURE` — base64 detached signature over the canonical
+  release-identity document built from `LAUNCH_RC_VERSION`,
+  `LAUNCH_ATTESTED_COMMIT`, `LAUNCH_ATTESTED_IMAGES`, `LAUNCH_MIGRATION_HEAD`,
+  `LAUNCH_BACKUP_ID`, `LAUNCH_OWNER`, `LAUNCH_ATTESTED_AT` and
+  `LAUNCH_ATTESTATION_EXPIRES` (exact bytes documented in
+  `apps/realtime/src/config.ts:canonicalLaunchAttestation`).
+
+The exact signed payload (UTF-8, LF separated) is:
+
+```text
+snowride-launch-attestation-v1
+rc=<rcVersion>
+commit=<attestedCommit>
+images=<attestedImages>
+migration=<migrationHead>
+backup=<backupId>
+owner=<owner>
+attested_at=<attestedAt>
+expires=<attestationExpires>
+```
+
+If the signature is missing, malformed, or does not verify over the exact
+identity, the gate stays closed. Example signing commands:
+
+```bash
+# canonical.txt holds the payload above with the real values.
+# Ed25519:
+openssl pkeyutl -sign -rawin -inkey owner.key -in canonical.txt -out sig.bin
+# RSA / ECDSA:
+openssl dgst -sha256 -sign owner.key -out sig.bin canonical.txt
+
+export LAUNCH_OWNER_SIGNATURE=$(base64 -w0 < sig.bin)
+export LAUNCH_OWNER_PUBLIC_KEY=$(openssl pkey -in owner.key -pubout)
+```
+
 ## First-time host
 
 1. `cp .env.example .env` and fill it in.
